You attacked the enemy, squeezed his throat and threatened him:
"If you don't lift this damn curse, I will kill you!"
The bastard helplessly floundered with his eyes wide open. His face already began to turn blue, when you weakened the grip. 
"I agree," he wheezed.
You released him. By shaking hands he opened some old book and quickly red the necessary passage. After giving this pathetic person a disdainful look, you left.
When you reached the city, you immediately called to the police and told them the address of a person who was running all over the city wearing a wolf skin. You knew that hunting those animals was banned, and there were a few pelts in the scoundrel's house that he personally bagged.
Soon you returned to your normal life, and those few days as a wolf, you tried to forget like a mere nightmare.